(173716, 9713, 2223, '<td valign="top">so beautiful!</td>', 'so beautiful!', '2002-12-16 17:47:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(173732, 9766, 3080, '<td valign="top">Definately naturally, untouched by man, but it''s not too greatly exciting.  Sorry.  It is technically well done.  lighting is good, and the angle and framing/cropping are good, and your focus seems good too.  It just lacks that something to make it scream ''wow'' to me.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Definately naturally, untouched by man, but it''s not too greatly exciting.  Sorry.  It is technically well done.  lighting is good, and the angle and framing/cropping are good, and your focus seems good too.  It just lacks that something to make it scream ''wow'' to me.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2002-12-16 18:03:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(173745, 9820, 4967, '<td valign="top">Good idea, and nice job of not having signs of man.  However I don''t think this photo is extremely visually appealing, and there is no real point that I can tell to look at.  I don''t care for the composition and I think this photo could have been done better.  I maybe would have approched this photo from a different angle.  You met the challenge, but I don''t care for the photo. -4</td>', 'Good idea, and nice job of not having signs of man.  However I don''t think this photo is extremely visually appealing, and there is no real point that I can tell to look at.  I don''t care for the composition and I think this photo could have been done better.  I maybe would have approched this photo from a different angle.  You met the challenge, but I don''t care for the photo. -4', '2002-12-16 18:43:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(173746, 9789, 4967, '<td valign="top">I find this photo to be both visually appealing, and well composed.  I absolutely love this photo, and the black and white looks wonderful.  Also I think the black border adds to the photo.l  Excellent macro!  This photo meets the challenge and manages to be beautiful at the same time.  No criticism here. -10</td>', 'I find this photo to be both visually appealing, and well composed.  I absolutely love this photo, and the black and white looks wonderful.  Also I think the black border adds to the photo.l  Excellent macro!  This photo meets the challenge and manages to be beautiful at the same time.  No criticism here. -10', '2002-12-16 18:47:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(173750, 9809, 4967, '<td valign="top">Interesting subject, but looks fairly dull to me.  I wish you would have pushed up the colors a little bit.  The focus looks a little bit soft on the entire subject, but just slightly.  The picture and composition isn''t all that appealing.  It fits the challenge, but I don''t care for it.  -4</td>', 'Interesting subject, but looks fairly dull to me.  I wish you would have pushed up the colors a little bit.  The focus looks a little bit soft on the entire subject, but just slightly.  The picture and composition isn''t all that appealing.  It fits the challenge, but I don''t care for it.  -4', '2002-12-16 18:56:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(173755, 9636, 4967, '<td valign="top">I think the subject on this photo is interesting, however I''m not sure if you should have had the blank spot so centered.  I think this would have worked quite well if you had included more of the trees in the bottom left, and less of them in the top right.  Just an idea though.  For the record I''d be interested to know whether these trees were planted to be like this or natural.  -6</td>', 'I think the subject on this photo is interesting, however I''m not sure if you should have had the blank spot so centered.  I think this would have worked quite well if you had included more of the trees in the bottom left, and less of them in the top right.  Just an idea though.  For the record I''d be interested to know whether these trees were planted to be like this or natural.  -6', '2002-12-16 19:10:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(173760, 9761, 4967, '<td valign="top">This is a cute photo, and I understand what your trying to say, but I don''t think this fits the challenge extremely well.  Faith must be taught in some way (by man) and the challenge was to have no obvious signs of man showing.  All the clothes were made by man, and even Santa was fabricated by man.  As far as the photo goes, kid pictures are always better when you get down on their level.  Also the background is extremely bothersome, I would have suggested using a different DOF, so you could blur out the background more.  Although I see how you could justify this picture for the challenge, I would have maybe tried to use something different, and while the photo has visual appeal, cute wise, I don''t care for it.  -3</td>', 'This is a cute photo, and I understand what your trying to say, but I don''t think this fits the challenge extremely well.  Faith must be taught in some way (by man) and the challenge was to have no obvious signs of man showing.  All the clothes were made by man, and even Santa was fabricated by man.  As far as the photo goes, kid pictures are always better when you get down on their level.  Also the background is extremely bothersome, I would have suggested using a different DOF, so you could blur out the background more.  Although I see how you could justify this picture for the challenge, I would have maybe tried to use something different, and while the photo has visual appeal, cute wise, I don''t care for it.  -3', '2002-12-16 19:29:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(173765, 9707, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met.  the square format works well, and i like that you managed to find a location where you are able to show the whole tree, and not just its top w/out the "hand of man" intruding.  i also like that the tree is almost a sillhouette, but there is still some detail visible.  centering it worked well for this photo.  just a nitpick, i would like to see the top of the tree, it looks like there''s not that much more missing.  overall, due to the weather (which is outside of your control, i know), the photo is just a little lacklustre in the color department.  but, still a decent entry.  :)</td>', 'challenge met.  the square format works well, and i like that you managed to find a location where you are able to show the whole tree, and not just its top w/out the "hand of man" intruding.  i also like that the tree is almost a sillhouette, but there is still some detail visible.  centering it worked well for this photo.  just a nitpick, i would like to see the top of the tree, it looks like there''s not that much more missing.  overall, due to the weather (which is outside of your control, i know), the photo is just a little lacklustre in the color department.  but, still a decent entry.  :)', '2002-12-16 19:34:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(173767, 9755, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met.  oh, man, i''m torn on this one.  i LOVE plain white backgrounds, and it works well, here, accentuating the branch and how it is completely covered in ice ... but the background looks unnatural.  i''m not suggesting you cheated, i know that you just have to find the right angle to take the photo ... but it looks less natural (my interpretation of the challenge) than it would with more plants in the background.  the clarity and focus and composition are all great.</td>', 'challenge met.  oh, man, i''m torn on this one.  i LOVE plain white backgrounds, and it works well, here, accentuating the branch and how it is completely covered in ice ... but the background looks unnatural.  i''m not suggesting you cheated, i know that you just have to find the right angle to take the photo ... but it looks less natural (my interpretation of the challenge) than it would with more plants in the background.  the clarity and focus and composition are all great.', '2002-12-16 19:36:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(173768, 9784, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met.  i love beaches, the patterns formed by the water washing the sand around objects in its path ... and you''ve captured a very nice photo here.  undisturbed sand is great.  i wonder why you chose to use b&amp;w instead of the warm colors of the sand and the different colors of the stones.  i think they would''ve earned you an extra point from me.  but, nevertheless, your entry is high on my list of favorites in this challenge so far!  :)</td>', 'challenge met.  i love beaches, the patterns formed by the water washing the sand around objects in its path ... and you''ve captured a very nice photo here.  undisturbed sand is great.  i wonder why you chose to use b&w instead of the warm colors of the sand and the different colors of the stones.  i think they would''ve earned you an extra point from me.  but, nevertheless, your entry is high on my list of favorites in this challenge so far!  :)', '2002-12-16 19:38:47.000000', NULL, 1),
